You are an expert iOS developer building "YoiYoi", a playful drinking tracker.

# Tech Stack
- iOS 17+, Swift 5.9+, SwiftUI, SwiftData (local), Firebase Firestore + Anonymous Auth (remote)
- Architecture: Feature-based MVVM with @Observable (iOS 17+)
- No UIKit, no Storyboard, no third-party UI libraries except Firebase SDK
- Localization: JA (default), EN via String Catalogs (.xcstrings) — designed for easy language addition

# Project documentation (repo root)
- Design system: `docs/DESIGN.md` — in Cursor use `@docs/DESIGN.md`
- Product spec & models: `docs/SPEC.md` — `@docs/SPEC.md`
- Implementation phases: `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — `@docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`

# Visual Design System (CRITICAL — follow docs/DESIGN.md; `@docs/DESIGN.md` in Cursor)
The app follows a professional design pattern inspired by modern card-based mobile UIs.

## Screen Structure (every screen follows this pattern):
1. **Wave Hero Area** (top ~35%): theme-color gradient clipped with WaveShape
   - Contains screen title (28pt Bold white) + primary content (meter, badges, etc.)
   - Home: coralRed hero with alcohol meter ring
   - Calendar: mintGreen hero with monthly summary badges
   - Feed: sunnyYellow hero (use charcoal text on yellow, NOT white)
   - Settings: lavender hero with profile card
2. **Content Area** (bottom ~65%): cream background with white ContentCards
   - First card overlaps the hero by -24px for visual connection
   - Cards use themed shadows (NEVER grey shadows)

## Card Types (use exactly these 3 types):
- **ContentCard**: white bg + themed shadow + radius 24 — for most information
- **GradientAccentCard**: horizontal gradient + radius 20 — for highlighted actions
- **FrostCard**: ultraThinMaterial + white overlay — only for overlays on hero areas

## Key Visual Rules:
- Shadows are ALWAYS tinted to match section theme color (opacity 0.10)
- Numbers use 28-48pt Heavy SF Pro Rounded for visual hierarchy
- Emoji (not SF Symbols) for all icons — keeps the playful tone
- No flat backgrounds — always use Wave Hero + cream content area
- Puffy buttons: top-light gradient + colored shadow + scale animation
- Cards appear with staggered opacity + offset(y:20) animation

# Multi-language Design
- MVP supports JA and EN only
- All language logic driven by `SupportedLanguage` enum
- Adding language: (1) enum case, (2) .xcstrings, (3) nickname JSONs, (4) font definition
- NO hardcoded language checks — always use SupportedLanguage

# Type-safe Alcohol Calculation
- ALWAYS use AlcoholByVolume type — NEVER pass raw Double for ABV
- UI percentage → AlcoholByVolume.fromPercentage()
- Code fraction → AlcoholByVolume.fromFraction()
- DrinkRecord init accepts AlcoholByVolume only
- Formula: volumeML × abv.fraction × 0.8 × numberOfDrinks

# Key Architecture Rules
- @Observable macro, not ObservableObject
- async/await, not Combine
- private(set) on all state
- Guard clauses over nested if-else
- MARK comments: State, Dependencies, Methods
- Max ~200 lines per file (split into sub-services if exceeding)
- All colors via AppColors enum — NEVER hardcode hex
- WaveHeroView is reusable — pass gradientColors + content via @ViewBuilder

# EULA
- Required before any onboarding step
- UserProfile stores eulaAccepted + eulaAcceptedAt
- EULA text from Resources/EULA/eula_{lang}.md

# Firebase Security
- Reactions: FieldValue.increment(1) + FieldValue.arrayUnion([uid])
- Rules enforce: add-only reacted_uids, +1 only reaction counts
- No Cloud Functions — all validation via security rules
- One reaction per user per post (rule + UI level)

# Business Rules
- Pure alcohol: volume(ml) × ABV(fraction) × 0.8
- Goals: men 40g/day 280g/week, women 20g/day 140g/week (MHLW Japan)
- No ads v1.0 (FeatureFlags.isAdsEnabled = false)
- No HealthKit, no IAP
- Feed posts are AUTO-GENERATED — zero free text
- Nicknames are PRESET-ONLY — zero free text
- Emoji reactions only: 👏🔥💪🫂🍀🍻, one per user per post

# Testing
- Test: AlcoholByVolume, DrinkRecord, AlcoholCalculator, FeedGenerator, Firestore rules
- NO: UI tests, ViewModel tests, performance tests in MVP
